# WS2d: the 2026-09-05 shape in one word — memory was freed and the machine did
# NOT get better, so swap "still" grew. The "still" only belongs when something
# was freed AND the verdict got no better (`worse`); flip that to `!worse` and the
# sentence says "still" exactly when it should not, dropping it from the case it
# exists for ("why did freeing 4 GB not help").
file: rust/banshee-core/src/pressure/deltas.rs
test: the_sentence_says_still_when_freeing_did_not_help
